.TH tkufilelist n 0.3 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkufilelist
.PP
A detail file list, filled from a storage provider. The list counterpart to \fBtkufiletree\fR: where the tree shows the hierarchy, the list shows the contents of one directory in columns \-\- name, modified, type, size and extension, chosen and ordered per option or by the user from a menu on the header. Directories come first, hidden entries follow the rules of the system, known extensions can be hidden, and one or several globs narrow the files. Tk 8.6+ and 9.x.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkufilelist::widget          path ?options?
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setDir          path dir     ;# show a directory
::tkutils::tkufilelist::dir             path         ;# current directory
::tkutils::tkufilelist::refresh         path         ;# re-read the directory
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setFilter       path glob    ;# one glob ("" = all files)
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setFilters      path globs   ;# several globs ({} = all)
::tkutils::tkufilelist::columns         path         ;# shown columns, in order
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setColumns      path keys    ;# show these, in this order
::tkutils::tkufilelist::allColumns                   ;# name mtime type size ext
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setShowHidden   path bool
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setHideExtensions path bool
::tkutils::tkufilelist::view            path         ;# the view as a dict
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setView         path dict    ;# apply a saved view
::tkutils::tkufilelist::selectedEntry   path         ;# entry dict of the selection, or ""
::tkutils::tkufilelist::selectedEntries path         ;# all selected entry dicts, in row order
.CE
.SS Options
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-provider\fR	local	a \fBtclutils::tuprovider\fR object
\fB\-dir\fR	\fB/\fR	the directory to show first
\fB\-show\fR	\fBboth\fR	\fBboth\fR, \fBfiles\fR or \fBdirs\fR
\fB\-files\fR	1	old form of \fB\-show\fR (0 = \fBdirs\fR)
\fB\-columns\fR	\fB{name mtime type size}\fR	columns and their order, from \fBname mtime type size ext\fR; \fBname\fR is always shown
\fB\-columnmenu\fR	1	right\-click on the header: a menu to show and hide columns
\fB\-showhidden\fR	0	show hidden entries
\fB\-showsystem\fR	0	also show hidden Windows system files
\fB\-hideextensions\fR	0	hide known extensions in the name (\fBreport.pdf\fR shows as \fBreport\fR)
\fB\-knownextensions\fR	a common list	the extensions that count as known (lower case, dot optional)
\fB\-dirsfirst\fR	1	directories before files, also after a click on a header
\fB\-timeformat\fR	\fB%d.%m.%Y %H:%M\fR	\fBclock format\fR of the Modified column
\fB\-sizeunits\fR	1000 on macOS, else 1024	1024 gives KB/MB (Windows), 1000 kB/MB (macOS)
\fB\-filter\fR	\fB""\fR	one glob for file names
\fB\-filters\fR	\fB{}\fR	several globs; a file shows when it matches any
\fB\-onactivate\fR		script, appended the entry dict \-\- double\-click / Enter
\fB\-onselect\fR		script, appended the entry dict \-\- selection change
\fB\-height\fR	16	visible rows
.TE
.SS Columns
.TS
l l l.
Key	Title	Shows
\fBname\fR	Name	the name, without a known extension under \fB\-hideextensions\fR
\fBmtime\fR	Modified	the modification time (\fB\-timeformat\fR)
\fBtype\fR	Type	\fBFolder\fR, \fBPDF file\fR, ..., \fBFile\fR without extension
\fBsize\fR	Size	the size, empty for folders (\fB\-sizeunits\fR)
\fBext\fR	Extension	the extension in lower case, without dot
.TE
.PP
The cells hold the raw values \-\- size in bytes, time in seconds \-\- and the table formats them, so a click on a header sorts by value, not by text. Directories stay in front (\fB\-dirsfirst\fR). Every column exists in the table; hidden ones can be switched on later without rebuilding it.
.SS "Hidden entries"
.PP
What is hidden depends on the system, as in its own file manager:
.IP \(bu
\fBWindows:\fR the \fIhidden\fR attribute; a leading dot means nothing (\fB.gitignore\fR is shown). A file that is hidden \fBand\fR has the \fIsystem\fR attribute (\fBdesktop.ini\fR, \fBpagefile.sys\fR) stays hidden until \fB\-showsystem 1\fR is given as well \-\- the Explorer's "Hide protected operating system files".
.IP \(bu
\fBLinux, macOS:\fR a leading dot.
.PP
The local provider reports this in the entry keys \fBhidden\fR and \fBsystem\fR (tclutils \fBtuprovider\fR 0.4). Other providers (ZIP, WebDAV, ...) do not, and then the leading dot decides.
.SS View
.PP
\fBview\fR returns \fBcolumns\fR, \fBshowhidden\fR, \fBhideextensions\fR, \fBsortcolumn\fR and \fBsortorder\fR as a dict; \fBsetView\fR applies one (missing keys stay as they are, an unknown column is dropped). \fBtkufiledialog \-app\fR stores the view per application this way.
.SS "Entry dicts"
.PP
Callbacks and \fBselectedEntry\fR hand back the provider's entry dict: \fBname\fR, \fBpath\fR, \fBtype\fR (\fBfile\fR/\fBdir\fR), \fBsize\fR, \fBmtime\fR, from the local provider also \fBhidden\fR and \fBsystem\fR. The entry travels with its row when the list is sorted.
.SS Use
.CS
package require tkutils::tkufilelist

::tkutils::tkufilelist::widget .list -dir [pwd] \
    -columns {name mtime size} -hideextensions 1 \
    -onactivate {apply {e {
        if {[dict get $e type] eq "dir"} {
            ::tkutils::tkufilelist::setDir .list [dict get $e path]
        }
    }}}
pack .list -fill both -expand 1
.CE
.SS Filtering
.PP
\fBsetFilter\fR takes one case\-insensitive glob, \fBsetFilters\fR a list of them; directories are never filtered, so navigation still works while a filter is active. \fB""\fR or \fB{}\fR clears it. The \fBctrlutils::cufilter\fR controller wires a text box to \fBsetFilter\fR.
.CS
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setFilters .list {*.pdf *.docx}   ;# PDF and Word files
::tkutils::tkufilelist::setFilter  .list ""               ;# everything again
.CE
.SS Texts
.PP
Titles and type names are English and go through \fBmsgcat\fR. An application translates them in the \fB::tkutils\fR namespace, for example in German:
.CS
namespace eval ::tkutils {
    foreach {en de} {Name Name Modified Geändert Type Typ Size Größe
            Extension Endung Folder Ordner File Datei "%s file" "%s-Datei"} {
        ::msgcat::mcset de $en $de
    }
}
.CE
.SS Provider\-backed
.PP
Because the list is filled through a provider, the same widget shows a local directory, the contents of a ZIP, or a WebDAV collection \-\- only the \fB\-provider\fR differs.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtkufiledialog\fR, \fBtkufiletree\fR, \fBtkupath\fR, \fBtclutils::tuprovider\fR
